§ `Third Schedule para 11 -- the cap`

#ASSERT `the most the CA can be liable for` `a forged signature an accredited CA handled correctly` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most the CA can be liable for` `a forged signature an accredited CA mishandled` EQUALS 500000
#ASSERT `the most the CA can be liable for` `a false identity in an accredited certificate` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the most the CA can be liable for` `a false identity in a certificate within the limit` EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT `the most the CA can be liable for` `a false identity where the CA waived the cap` EQUALS 500000
#ASSERT `the most the CA can be liable for` `a false identity in an unaccredited CA's certificate` EQUALS 500000

§ `Third Schedule paras 16, 18, 5`

#ASSERT `the CA must suspend the certificate` `the subscriber` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the CA must suspend the certificate` `a person duly authorised by the subscriber` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the CA must suspend the certificate` `a person acting for a subscriber who is unavailable` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the CA must suspend the certificate` `a person acting for a subscriber who is available` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the CA must suspend the certificate` `a stranger` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the CA must suspend the certificate` `the subscriber` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the CA must suspend the certificate` `the subscriber` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the CA must notify the subscriber of the revocation` `a material fact in the certificate is false`
